From ce08e56ddcb56677450530899999898e7cc65910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:22:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Tools_OtherSettings: drop the Asusnat tunnel toggle - it is
 provably inert

"Disable Asusnat tunnel" (aae_disable_force) offered to disable a daemon this
firmware does not contain:

  - natnl_api.o is compiled only under `ifeq ($(RTCONFIG_TUNNEL),y)`
    (rc/Makefile:1057), and .config carries `# RTCONFIG_TUNNEL is not set`, so
    all three of its aae_disable_force checks are compiled out
  - watchdog's mastiff_check() sits inside `#ifdef RTCONFIG_TUNNEL`, likewise out
  - no mastiff, aaeuac or natnl binary exists anywhere in the staged image

restart_mastiff goes with it: that service was in this page's action_script
solely for this control, so every save was restarting something that is not
there. The nvram entry stays in defaults.c - an unused key costs nothing and
removing it would churn the table for no gain.

THE OTHER ROW IS NOT INERT AND IS DELIBERATELY KEPT. "Redirect webui access"
(http_dut_redir) has a complete, working, LAN-LOCAL implementation:
Main_Login.asp fetches <Web_DOMAIN_NAME>:<port>/chdom.json, and that endpoint is
served BY THE ROUTER - www/chdom.json exists, is registered in web.c
mime_handlers, and is backed by ej_chdom(). It is a hostname-vs-IP convenience,
not telemetry, and it is off by default. Removing it would delete a feature that
works.

Worth recording for the next de-cloud audit: reaper_verify check 17 greps the
staged www for an ASUS host in a request-shaped position, and it cannot see this
line - the host comes from the <#Web_DOMAIN_NAME#> dict token, not a literal, so
the URL only exists after substitution. Check 17 passing is not evidence that a
page makes no ASUS-hostname request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Tools_OtherSettings.asp | 9 +--------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Tools_OtherSettings.asp b/release/src/router/www/Tools_OtherSettings.asp
index 1b0048d221..0d68a251ad 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Tools_OtherSettings.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Tools_OtherSettings.asp
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ function applyRule(){
 <input type="hidden" name="next_page" value="Tools_OtherSettings.asp">
 <input type="hidden" name="modified" value="0">
 <input type="hidden" name="action_mode" value="apply">
-<input type="hidden" name="action_script" value="restart_conntrack;restart_mastiff">
+<input type="hidden" name="action_script" value="restart_conntrack">
 <input type="hidden" name="action_wait" value="5">
 <input type="hidden" name="first_time" value="">
 <input type="hidden" name="SystemCmd" value="">
@@ -311,13 +311,6 @@ function applyRule(){
 							<input type="radio" name="ipv6_ns_drop" class="input" value="0" <% nvram_match_x("", "ipv6_ns_drop", "0", "checked"); %>><#checkbox_No#>
 						</td>
 					</tr>
-					<tr>
-						<th>Disable Asusnat tunnel</th>
-						<td>
-							<input type="radio" name="aae_disable_force" class="input" value="1" <% nvram_match_x("", "aae_disable_force", "1", "checked"); %>><#checkbox_Yes#>
-							<input type="radio" name="aae_disable_force" class="input" value="0" <% nvram_match_x("", "aae_disable_force", "0", "checked"); %>><#checkbox_No#>
-						</td>
-					</tr>
 					<tr>
 						<th><a class="hintstyle" href="javascript:void(0);" onClick="openHint(50,21);">dhcpd: send empty WPAD with a carriage return</a></th>
 						<td>
